WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
Here's a quick way to turn AI output into professional,

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.600
print-ready PDF files.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.000
Used well, AI saves real time on handouts,

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.400
quizzes, and exit tickets.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.900
But here's how most of us use it.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:15.600
We ask AI a question,

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.100
copy the text, and paste it into a document.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.200
Let's see how that goes.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.800
Part 1, the usual way.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:27.900
We ask Gemini for a four-question exit ticket on the quadratic formula.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:31.900
We want professional formatting that fits on one page.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.300
Inside the chat window it looks great.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:38.400
Clean equations, clear sections, and even an answer key.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:41.200
So we copy the response.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.100
And paste it into Google Docs.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.400
Let's take a closer look.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:48.200
Every equation comes through as raw code.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:52.400
Dollar signs, backslashes, and formatting commands are everywhere.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:55.200
That's not something you'd hand to students.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:58.000
Part 2, the better way.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.200
This time we'll ask for LaTeX.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:04.300
LaTeX is the typesetting language behind textbooks and math journals.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:08.100
You don't need to learn it because the AI writes it for you.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:11.400
We use the same prompt as before with one extra line.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:14.000
Output this in LaTeX code.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.000
Now instead of formatted text,

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:20.600
Gemini writes the entire exit ticket as LaTeX code.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:23.500
Click the copy button on the code block.

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:27.200
Then open Overleaf, a free online LaTeX editor.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:31.200
Paste the code into a blank project and hit recompile.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:34.100
In seconds it compiles into a finished document.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:36.700
Just download the PDF.

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:38.200
And here's the result.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:39.900
Properly typeset equations,

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:44.000
clean answer blanks and a layout that's ready to print.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:49.000
Same AI and the same prompt with a completely different result.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.300
So next time prompt your AI and ask for LaTeX.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:55.400
Paste it into Overleaf and download your PDF.

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:56.900
Thanks for watching.

